course: dictionary
lesson: 13953
title: Licensed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Licensed means having official permission to do something. Someone in charge has checked and said yes, you may do this. «Only a licensed driver may drive a car on the road.» The word tells you the driver has passed the tests and been given permission to drive.
explain: The word can also describe things, not just people. «The toy robot is a licensed product.» A licensed toy uses a famous film or cartoon character with the owner's permission, so it is made properly, not copied. Look at the words around licensed to see what it describes: a person, a shop, a toy or a taxi.
explain: Some phrases come up again and again: «licensed to drive», «fully licensed», «a licensed taxi». Fully means completely, so «fully licensed» means every permission is in place. To check your meaning, swap in "allowed by the official rules" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Licensed means having official permission.
fact: «Licensed to drive» means you have been given official permission to drive.
fact: A licensed taxi has official permission to carry passengers.
fact: A licensed toy uses a famous character with the owner's permission.
fact: License is a verb meaning to give official permission. Its forms are license, licenses, licensed and licensing.
exercise: «Only a licensed driver may drive a car on the road.» What does licensed mean here? | Very fast and careful | Painted in bright colours | Tired and sleepy | *Having official permission
exercise: «The toy robot is a licensed product.» What does licensed tell you about the robot? | It can fly | It is very old | It is made of wood | *It uses a famous character with permission
exercise: Mia says «fully licensed» means half allowed. What does «fully licensed» really mean? | *Has all the permission it needs | Is very large | Has no permission at all | Is paid for in full
test: What does «licensed to drive» mean? | *Has official permission to drive | Drives a bus to school | Likes driving fast | Cannot drive at all
test: «The council will license the new café next month.» Which word means give official permission? | café | *license | month | council
exam: Which sentence uses licensed to mean having official permission? | The licensed sky was blue. | The licensed sandwich was very tasty. | I licensed my bike to the park. | *Only a licensed doctor can give this medicine.
